{
  "title": "[MPS]torch.compileResNet-18 model fails duringloss.backward()on MPS backend, but works on CPU",
  "issue_id": "161905",
  "bug_description": "### 🐛 Describe the bug\n\n#### 🐛 Bug\n\nWhen using `torch.compile` on a model that has been moved to the `mps` device on macOS, calling `loss.backward()` results in a runtime error. The forward pass completes without issues.\n\nNotably, the exact same code runs successfully without any errors when the model and data are on the `cpu` backend. This suggests a potential bug or unimplemented feature in the `torch.compile` support for the MPS backend, specifically concerning the backward pass (gradient computation).\n\n#### To Reproduce\n\nHere is a minimal, self-contained code snippet to reproduce the error:\n\n```python\nimport torch\nimport torch.nn as nn\nimport torch.optim as optim\nfrom torch import Tensor\nfrom typing import Type, Any, Callable, Union, List, Optional\nfrom torchvision.models.resnet import resnet18\n\n\nBATCH_SIZE = 4\nNUM_CLASSES = 10\nLEARNING_RATE = 0.01\ndevice='mps'\n\nmodel = resnet18(num_classes=NUM_CLASSES)\n\ncriterion = nn.CrossEntropyLoss()\noptimizer = optim.SGD(model.parameters(), lr=LEARNING_RATE)\n\nmodel=model.to(device)\nmodel.train() \n\n@torch.compile\ndef train(images,labels):\n    images=images.to(device)\n    labels=labels.to(device)\n    \n    optimizer.zero_grad()\n\n    outputs = model(images)\n    loss = criterion(outputs, labels)\n    loss.backward()\n    optimizer.step()\n\nimages = torch.randn(BATCH_SIZE, 3, 224, 224)\nlabels = torch.randint(0, NUM_CLASSES, (BATCH_SIZE,))\n\ntrain(images,labels)\n```\n\n#### Expected behavior\n\nThe code should execute without any errors, regardless of whether the `DEVICE` is set to `'mps'` or `'cpu'`. The `loss.backward()` call should complete successfully, and the gradients for the model's parameters should be computed.\n\n#### Actual behavior\n\nWhen `DEVICE = 'mps'`, the code fails at `loss.backward()` with a runtime error. The forward pass and loss calculation are successful.\n\n### Error logs\n\n```\nW0901 19:47:33.366000 11122 site-packages/torch/_inductor/utils.py:2241] [0/0_1] DeviceCopy in input program\nW0901 19:47:33.367000 11122 site-packages/torch/_inductor/utils.py:2241] [0/0_1] DeviceCopy in input program\nW0901 19:47:34.821000 11122 site-packages/torch/_inductor/utils.py:1554] [1/0_1] Not enough SMs to use max_autotune_gemm mode\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/Users/name/resnet.py\", line 37, in <module>\n    train(images,labels)\n  File \"/opt/homebrew/Caskroom/miniconda/base/envs/mlxnn/lib/python3.10/site-packages/torch/_dynamo/eval_frame.py\", line 830, in compile_wrapper\n    return fn(*args, **kwargs)\n  File \"/Users/name/resnet.py\", line 27, in train\n    optimizer.zero_grad()\n  File \"/Users/name/resnet.py\", line 31, in torch_dynamo_resume_in_train_at_27\n    loss.backward()\n  File \"/opt/homebrew/Caskroom/miniconda/base/envs/mlxnn/lib/python3.10/site-packages/torch/_tensor.py\", line 625, in backward\n    torch.autograd.backward(\n  File \"/opt/homebrew/Caskroom/miniconda/base/envs/mlxnn/lib/python3.10/site-packages/torch/autograd/__init__.py\", line 354, in backward\n    _engine_run_backward(\n  File \"/opt/homebrew/Caskroom/miniconda/base/envs/mlxnn/lib/python3.10/site-packages/torch/autograd/graph.py\", line 841, in _engine_run_backward\n    return Variable._execution_engine.run_backward(  # Calls into the C++ engine to run the backward pass\n  File \"/opt/homebrew/Caskroom/miniconda/base/envs/mlxnn/lib/python3.10/site-packages/torch/autograd/function.py\", line 315, in apply\n    return user_fn(self, *args)\n  File \"/opt/homebrew/Caskroom/miniconda/base/envs/mlxnn/lib/python3.10/site-packages/torch/_functorch/_aot_autograd/runtime_wrappers.py\", line 2303, in backward\n    return impl_fn()\n  File \"/opt/homebrew/Caskroom/miniconda/base/envs/mlxnn/lib/python3.10/site-packages/torch/_functorch/_aot_autograd/runtime_wrappers.py\", line 2289, in impl_fn\n    out = CompiledFunction._backward_impl(ctx, all_args)\n  File \"/opt/homebrew/Caskroom/miniconda/base/envs/mlxnn/lib/python3.10/site-packages/torch/_functorch/_aot_autograd/runtime_wrappers.py\", line 2423, in _backward_impl\n    out = call_func_at_runtime",
